# The owner is a required reviewer ONLY for (a) guardrails: a file whose silent
# weakening would stop an agent guardrail or a required check protecting us, and
# (b) human-facing documents written for other people. Everything else lands on
# agent review plus green CI, sensitive or not (owner ruling).
#
# GitHub applies the LAST matching pattern, so order is the mechanism: owned
# paths first, then lines that name no owner and so release documents and
# discovery files, then the shared lines from templates/codeowners, which stay
# last (SYNC-1). There is no catch-all line, by design.
#
# This repo does not require code-owner review (REPO-1), so these lines request
# a review and do not block a merge by themselves; the merge route reads them.
# tools/tests/codeowners_ownership.py checks a fixed table of sample paths
# against this file, and it runs in CI through `pnpm selftest`.

# (a) Guardrails: the workflows that enforce this repo's required checks or
# publish a release (ci.yml carries the self-test and the dogfood job;
# publish.yml checks the tag's signature before it publishes). The reusable gate
# and the docs-lint caller come from the shared lines. repo-settings-audit.yml
# and the Dependabot settings are released: nothing requires them, and
# tools/tests/run.sh fails if the audit stops running.
/.github/workflows/ci.yml            @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.github/workflows/publish.yml       @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
# The code of every gate other repos run, the floors and
# exemption definitions they read, and the tests of those gates.
/tools/                              @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
# Ruleset definitions, the CODEOWNERS template and the file that sets how it is
# compared, and the workflow templates.
/templates/rulesets/                 @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/templates/org-rulesets/             @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/templates/codeowners                @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/templates/manifest.tsv              @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/templates/workflows/                @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
# The TS-4 floor tiers, which tools/check-tsconfig.sh reads directly.
/packages/tsconfig/*.json            @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
# The root package.json holds the selftest script that runs every gate test;
# changing it could stop them running. A root dependency bump reaches the owner
# for that reason; package.json files under packages/ and the lockfile do not.
/package.json                        @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
# (b) Human-facing documents: legal text and the pages written for other people.
/LICENSE                             @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/LICENSE-DOCS                        @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/NOTICE                              @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/README.md                           @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/CONTRIBUTING.md                     @branchLeft/branchleft-admin

# Released: engineering documents and a discovery file that judges nothing.
# These name no owner and come after the owned directories so they win.
/tools/**/*.md
/templates/**/*.md
/tools/clause-paths.tsv

# Owned again, after the releases, so a document extension never releases the
# rulebook, a CODEOWNERS file or a floor file at any depth.
CLAUDE.md                            @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
AUTHORISATIONS.md                    @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
**/CODEOWNERS                        @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
**/floors.tsv                        @branchLeft/branchleft-admin

# Shared lines from templates/codeowners. They stay last (SYNC-1).
/.standardsignore        @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.standards.mode         @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.docs-lint*             @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.standards-db-tooling   @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.github/CODEOWNERS      @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.github/workflows/standards.yml  @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.github/workflows/docs-lint.yml  @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
